From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:50:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xodus: Receive whole frames, and fail requests that time out
 after 30 seconds.

The socket thread read into a 2048-byte buffer, while a frame carries up to 65535 bytes after its
8-byte header (an MSA token response is about 3.3 KB). Once the buffer was full, recv() was asked
for 0 bytes, returned 0, and the thread took it for a disconnection. Size the buffer for the
largest frame.

A request that got no reply returned HRESULT_FROM_NT(STATUS_TIMEOUT), a success code; return
HRESULT_FROM_WIN32(ERROR_TIMEOUT). Wait 30 seconds instead of 5: requests the service answers
with Microsoft's services, such as a game license, can take 10.

Original work for macrock (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

Topic: xodus-protocol
---
 src/Xodus/IPCLayer.cpp | 2 +-
 src/private.h          | 6 ++++--
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Xodus/IPCLayer.cpp b/src/Xodus/IPCLayer.cpp
index babdb4ec464952b2e0e86f73a8efb78f448a836c..7879a4efaa82a2ed5a82ea8c1a0ac43fb7e6d275 100644
--- a/src/Xodus/IPCLayer.cpp
+++ b/src/Xodus/IPCLayer.cpp
@@ -447,7 +447,7 @@ private:
         if ( asyncres )
         {
             WARN("Timeout while waiting for %p to respond.\n", handler);
-            return HRESULT_FROM_NT( STATUS_TIMEOUT );
+            return HRESULT_FROM_WIN32( ERROR_TIMEOUT );
         }
 
         *result = context.response;
diff --git a/src/private.h b/src/private.h
index 0207461cb1b883624d4756581ca5e3e5645adbeb..b71f3bf1fefce32f3c8a2bf851cfca46515af57d 100644
--- a/src/private.h
+++ b/src/private.h
@@ -69,8 +69,10 @@
 #include "windows.system.profile.h"
 
 #define XODUS_SOCKET_SUFFIX "xodus.sock"
-#define POLL_BUFFER_SIZE 2048
-#define IPC_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS 5000
+/* A whole frame: the 8-byte header and the largest message its 16-bit length allows. */
+#define POLL_BUFFER_SIZE (8 + 0xffff)
+/* Game license replies can take 10 s. */
+#define IPC_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS 30000
 
 #define E_ILLEGAL_METHOD_CALL                              _HRESULT_TYPEDEF_(0x8000000E)
 
